=====================

 S~S  Release notes version 260216: basis for "SimpleSal App bringup", which is "app-events".

------------------------------------------

    SimpleSal App "app-events" published to demonstrate ssTEA concepts and functionality.

    The 1-second output to the serial port shows Time progressing, the Built-In LED is turned ON
    at the start of a 5-second period, and then an Event occurs 3 seconds later to turn it OFF.

    The 1-second output and 5-second LED off->on transition are controlled by classic Arduino Time.
    The 3-second LED on-off transition is controlled by an ssTEA Event granted Agency to execute.

    This App also demonstrates the shared data space between the co-existing App and ssTEA software.

------------------------------------------

    The first release was completed into a properly function SimpleSal App, and then the
    software was modified to not work.  The modifications will be explored, one change and
    release through the repository at a time.  This will demonstrate ssTEA development/debug tools.

------------------------------------------

    The intention is to demonstrate the hidden complexities within ssTEA that support the main
    educational goal.  Extensive explanatory messages are enabled in the failing version simply
    to show how ssTEA explanatory messages communicate the condition of the App to the developer.

    The change from nonworking to working will eliminate many of the messages during init State;
    then the periodic display of the ssTEA API information for each Event will show how ssTEA works.

    The App with messages fully enabled may hide the signal for the serial port each period.

